- C library: compiles successfully; PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH = 9, PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODEUNIT = 112 ('p'). i.e. C treats the whole thing as the 9 literal characters `p { W o m b a t }`.
- Rust library: compiles successfully but PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH = 8 and PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODEUNIT = 123 ('{'). i.e. Rust drops the `p` and produces only 8 literals `{ W o m b a t }`.

ROOT CAUSE TO LOOK FOR: the off-by-one on the pointer restore in the ESCAPE_FAILED path of the pattern pre-parse (parse_regex). Here is the exact C ground truth from c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c around line 3592-3606 (in the main `switch(c)` of the parsing loop, `case CHAR_BACKSLASH:`):

